{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":285768,"duration_api_ms":284470,"num_turns":29,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"561051a9-a254-4fbc-a123-f0122457c28b","total_cost_usd":1.59537975,"usage":{"input_tokens":16,"cache_creation_input_tokens":109075,"cache_read_input_tokens":1202162,"output_tokens":12500,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":109075,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":12500,"cacheReadInputTokens":1202162,"cacheCreationInputTokens":109075,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.59537975,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"In nitrogen_cycle.rs, the local `concentration_from_total()` function (line 383-389) exactly duplicates the private `concentration()` function in water.rs (line 301-307). Extract this shared logic to a `pub(crate)` function (e.g., in water.rs or a shared utilities module) so there is a single canonical implementation. Currently, if the safety checks (NaN/Inf handling, EPSILON threshold, non-negativity clamping) are updated in one copy, the other copy silently diverges.","rationale":"The task's stated goal is 'one canonical place' for concentration math. Having two identical private implementations in different modules undermines that. A future developer updating the safety logic in water.rs would reasonably not know about the copy in nitrogen_cycle.rs."},{"body":"algae_growth.rs uses `state.water.tan_mg_n_per_l(volume_l)` (the WaterState method taking volume_l directly) while plant_growth.rs, shrimp.rs, events.rs, and snapshot.rs use `state.concentrations()` (the ConcentrationView pattern). Standardize algae_growth.rs to use `state.concentrations()` like the other systems, so the volume is computed once via the canonical `water_volume_l()` path and the calling pattern is consistent across all systems.","rationale":"Inconsistent patterns across systems that were all migrated in the same changeset make it harder for reviewers of dependent tasks (e.g., tanksim-6e5.2.5, normalizing algae kinetics) to know which pattern to follow. Both paths produce the same result, so this is a low-risk consistency fix."}],"summary":"The implementation is correct and well-tested. All nine required concentration helpers (TAN, nitrite, nitrate, DOC, DIC, DO, phosphate, alkalinity, water_volume_l) are present with correct naming. The ConcentrationView pattern cleanly separates volume computation from repeated concentration queries. Edge cases (zero volume from full substrate displacement, empty geometry, very large tanks) are handled gracefully by returning 0.0. A proptest confirms outputs are never negative across wide input ranges. The save migration (v2→v3) correctly rescales dissolved totals from gross-volume to net-volume semantics. All major process systems (nitrogen cycle, plant growth, algae, shrimp, dissolved oxygen, events, microfauna, snapshot) have been migrated to use the new helpers. The legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l conversion for Monod half-saturation constants is clearly documented as a transitional pattern. Two minor issues found: (1) a duplicated concentration-from-total helper in nitrogen_cycle.rs, and (2) inconsistent helper calling conventions between algae_growth.rs and other systems. No bugs, safety issues, or correctness gaps identified."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c03c65d2-034e-4772-8f8f-faf2f6e0f40c"}
